<!--
  The mark of the EGX 33 Shariah index: a solid eight-pointed star with a crescent cut out of it.

  Solid since 2026-11-12. It was an outlined star holding a thin crescent and a small five-pointed
  star, and at the 13dp it was drawn at the 9-unit stroke came out near 0.6dp - invisible in both
  themes. A filled shape with one bold cut is what survives being drawn the size of a letter.

  One path, nonZero, and the direction each piece is traced in is what cuts it. The star runs
  clockwise (+1), the crescent's outer disc anticlockwise (-1) and its inner disc clockwise (+1):
  the crescent nets to zero and is the hole, and the edge of the inner disc that pokes past the
  outer one nets to +2 and stays filled. evenOdd would have cut that edge too, as a second sliver.
  Drawn on a 200-unit grid rather than Material's 24, because the star's vertices land on fractions
  a 24-grid rounds into a visibly lopsided shape.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="200"
    android:viewportHeight="200">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF000000"
        android:fillType="nonZero"
        android:pathData="M100,6L127,37L164,36L163,73L194,100L163,127L164,164L127,163L100,194L73,163L36,164L37,127L6,100L37,73L36,36L73,37Z M48,104A48,48 0 1,0 144,104A48,48 0 1,0 48,104Z M74,94A40,40 0 1,1 154,94A40,40 0 1,1 74,94Z" />
</vector>
